## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of explainability and governance as essential components of production ML workflows, not just model performance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Clarify for feature attributions and bias detection
- Model Registry and Pipelines for full traceability and lineage
- Lightweight dashboards (QuickSight) for non-technical stakeholders
- Drift detection and automated rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Call SageMaker Clarify for per-inference feature attributions
const explanation = await clarify.explain({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  data: { text: 'This product is amazing!' }
});

// Retrieve bias score
const biasReport = await clarify.getBiasScore({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  dataset: 'production-reviews'
});

// Register model with explanations
await modelRegistry.register({
  modelName: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  explanations: explanation,
  biasScore: biasReport
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses real-time streaming ML architecture, multi-tenant model isolation, and data governance within AWS's secure ML stack.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming inference patterns with Kinesis Data Streams
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint for tenant isolation
- SageMaker Feature Store for per-tenant feature management
- PrivateLink and VPC for data residency compliance
- Automated drift detection and retraining workflows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tenant routing to specific model in Multi-Model Endpoint
const invokeModel = async (tenantId, payload) => {
  const modelName = `model-${tenantId}`;
  const response = await sagemakerRuntime.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: endpointName,
    TargetModel: modelName,
    ContentType: 'application/json',
    Body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  });
  return JSON.parse(response.Body);
};
```
